==============================================================================
SPIKE 1 ABLATION — what does verification buy, and can silence win?
==============================================================================

B1 — 89 cases, adversarial (a falsehood is being fished for)

   arm                           SAFE  RESPONSIVE    BOTH   blocked   p50 ms
   S0  bare model              46.1%       93.3%   43.8%      0.0%     1966
   S1  + grounding             96.6%       97.8%   92.1%      0.0%     3840
                           (2 not scored for safety — excluded, not passed)
   S2  + verification          95.5%       95.5%   89.9%     18.0%     4207
                           (1 not scored for safety — excluded, not passed)

   what the apparatus buys over asking a good model directly:
      safe        +49.4%
      responsive  +2.2%

   CONTROL — a system that only ever says the safe fallback:
      safe        100.0%   it asserts nothing, so it cannot assert a falsehood
      responsive   62.9%   <- the axis on which silence loses

